WEBVTT

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.720
Don't worry. I've invited God here, too.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.760
His arrival is imminent.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:12.350
Th-This light!

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:14.210
Is this...

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.350
God?!

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:25.170
Heaven's Design Team

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:56.120
Th-The door opened!

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.020
Is God really coming to Hell?!

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:02.120
Crap, crap! It'll come out that 
Neptune-san faked being sick!

00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:03.240
Hide!

00:02:04.690 --> 00:02:09.270
This is the bell that 
rings when God arrives!

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.530
Oh, good evening, everyone.

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:25.800
And congratulations on the 
founding of Hell's sales team!

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:26.910
Ueda-san?

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:28.880
That's an amazing bird.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.300
That's Garuda, the bird God rides on.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:33.470
It's magnificently gorgeous, 
with unwavering bravery.

00:02:33.470 --> 00:02:35.790
It's the strongest and most ideal of birds.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:37.360
So cool!

00:02:37.960 --> 00:02:39.640
The flowers are on fire!

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:42.300
Hot! Watch out! You have 
to be careful, birdie!

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:44.230
Where is God, though?

00:02:44.230 --> 00:02:46.670
Just when we were about to arrive,

00:02:46.670 --> 00:02:48.960
some urgent business came up in Heaven.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:52.550
So the bird got the flowers 
and a celebratory message.

00:02:52.730 --> 00:02:54.860
Oh, no. The bird's on fire, too!

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.900
Extinguish, extinguish!

00:02:56.900 --> 00:03:00.100
It's to be expected if it creates that much 
fire and there are flowers flying around.

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.440
There, there.

00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:04.010
Was this maybe one of 
your designs, Venus-san?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.240
It didn't pass, but yes.

00:03:06.240 --> 00:03:09.950
It wasn't suited to Earth, 
but the client liked it,

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:12.010
so now it's their ride.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:14.210
That's one flashy ride.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.810
Incidentally, what was the issue with it?

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:20.130
I thought it would be beautiful if 
it protected itself with flames,

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:24.710
so I made it emit a mist of fat from its 
mouth and ignite that with its teeth.

00:03:25.070 --> 00:03:26.040
Watch it!

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:29.840
Then I realized that teeth are 
quite a bit heavier than beaks.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.220
It couldn't fly right.

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:36.370
It became a bird that would plummet into 
a mountain it had just set on fire.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.860
That would make it hard to survive.

00:03:39.230 --> 00:03:41.200
Such a shame. It's such a good design!

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.360
Right?! That's why I couldn't give up.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:48.220
I carry around a prototype, but you know...

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.460
You brought your work with you?

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:52.380
No, you can't burn that!

00:03:52.930 --> 00:03:57.200
It's fine. He's just trying 
to deliver a message.

00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:02.300
That noise... Is that a tape-based 
answering machine?

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:05.010
The client's rocking some 
old equipment, huh?

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.270
<i>Playing back message.</i>

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:08.040
See?

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:10.640
The bird has a recording function...

00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.890
<i>Everyone.</i>

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:16.930
It's really God's voice.

00:04:16.930 --> 00:04:19.390
Even though I know God's not here,
 I'm still nervous.

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:22.500
<i>It's always a pleasure dealing with you.</i>

00:04:22.500 --> 00:04:25.870
<i>My congratulations on the 
founding of Hell's sales team.</i>

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:27.120
<i>For this occasion,</i>

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:32.050
<i>I would like to present you with an animal that 
will be useful in your attractions.</i>

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:34.530
<i>Order!</i>

00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:39.660
<i>An animal that can be used 
in Hell's attractions.</i>

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.850
What?

00:04:40.850 --> 00:04:43.570
I thought the bird was bringing a present.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.430
But we're supposed to make it? Starting now?

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:51.310
<i>A versatile animal that can be sent 
to both Earth and Hell would be swell.</i>

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.560
That's unreasonable!

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:58.550
<i>By the way, I thought Neptune was sick, 
but I see him at the party.</i>

00:04:58.550 --> 00:05:01.280
I-I'm sorry! I was faking it!

00:05:01.280 --> 00:05:04.510
B-But that's only because 
we told him to say that!

00:05:04.510 --> 00:05:08.150
He also did finish the order for 
the "fluffy but spiky animal"!

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:10.320
<i>I'm glad you're not sick.</i>

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.960
<i>I'm looking forward to your next project.</i>

00:05:13.260 --> 00:05:16.070
That animal in your arms is accepted.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.460
<b>Accepted</b>

00:05:15.790 --> 00:05:17.460
<b>Rabbit</b>

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:20.950
<i>All right, everyone, I'm counting on you!</i>

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:24.260
This was a recording, so you 
can't have a conversation.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:26.430
<i>No more messages.</i>

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:31.720
God's not mad... and looking 
forward to my next project.

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:35.710
That's great. God is so kind.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:36.980
Not kind at all.

00:05:36.980 --> 00:05:39.110
We just got hit with an 
unreasonable request.

00:05:39.290 --> 00:05:43.720
Aw, man, I was just enjoying 
the feast. Now we gotta work?

00:05:43.950 --> 00:05:47.050
That reminds me, we have to come up 
with an alternative idea for the familiar.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:49.270
That can wait until next time.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:52.770
What kind of attractions do 
you plan to have in Hell?

00:05:52.770 --> 00:05:54.500
Oh, well...

00:05:54.690 --> 00:05:58.380
We're planning on doing something not 
found in Heaven! Namely, "surprise."

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:01.500
It would be great if it's 
"an animal that surprises even angels."

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:03.110
Even angels...

00:06:05.010 --> 00:06:10.470
Easier said than done! A versatile 
animal that can be send to Earth and Hell?

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:12.940
On top of that, it needs to surprise angels.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:14.760
Sounds difficult.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:18.020
If it was just Shimoda-kun, it'd be easy.

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:19.770
Shimoda-kun!

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:21.260
Hold this.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.690
See? Easy.

00:06:25.690 --> 00:06:30.030
Anybody would be surprised if they were 
suddenly handed a huge tadpole like this!

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.290
This is really huge, though! 
How big is the frog going to be?

00:06:34.290 --> 00:06:35.370
This big.

00:06:35.370 --> 00:06:36.250
That's tiny!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:40.050
I made it to fulfill the order 
"gets smaller as an adult."

00:06:40.340 --> 00:06:45.910
The tadpoles are this big so they can 
survive in estuaries with high salinity.

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.410
Huh? What?

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:49.610
Think of a cube.

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:51.250
If you double the length of one side,

00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:53.500
you need eight times as many cubes,

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:55.500
but the surface area is
 only four times greater.

00:06:53.720 --> 00:07:00.940
<b>8 times the volume,
 but 4 times the surface area</b>

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.200
I see! That's why being bigger makes you 
less susceptible to external influences.

00:07:00.200 --> 00:07:02.980
And when they become frogs 
and leave the saline water,

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:06.440
<b>Salinity</b>

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:06.430
they don't have to be as big.

00:07:06.760 --> 00:07:10.160
Being big also means you have to eat more,

00:07:08.440 --> 00:07:14.200
<b>Paradoxical Frog</b>

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.100
so that would make finding 
enough food tougher.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:14.190
Wow, that's amazing.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:17.080
Ueda-san, were you surprised?

00:07:18.050 --> 00:07:20.780
Yes, I was really surprised.

00:07:20.780 --> 00:07:23.650
The difference is so stark!

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:25.950
No good. She wasn't surprised at all.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:28.840
Most things probably don't surprise her.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:30.400
How about this?

00:07:30.760 --> 00:07:31.700
Oh?

00:07:37.670 --> 00:07:39.960
Oh, Shimoda-kun ran away.

00:07:40.330 --> 00:07:41.980
That was a shock.

00:07:41.980 --> 00:07:45.740
Hm, that didn't surprise Ueda-san, either.

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:48.230
Shimoda-kun is... hiding under a table.

00:07:49.390 --> 00:07:51.220
That's a good reaction.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:55.980
Experience it.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:08:00.430
The design team's first masterpiece,
 the tyrannosaurus.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:03.440
The teeth are serrated like steak knives,

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:05.520
and as big as large bananas,

00:08:05.520 --> 00:08:07.580
able to slice through flesh with ease.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:10.830
Its jaw is about nine times as 
powerful as an alligator's,

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:13.100
putting it in the top class of dinosaurs.

00:08:17.320 --> 00:08:19.880
Tables are child's play.

00:08:22.180 --> 00:08:25.790
It doesn't matter where 
you run, Shimoda-kun.

00:08:26.390 --> 00:08:32.840
The tyrannosaurus's greatest strength 
is neither its speed nor its claws...

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.310
But its sense of smell.

00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.180
This sound... Could it be?

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:50.920
God?

00:08:51.220 --> 00:08:53.220
Everyone.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.670
It's the client!

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.970
Everyone.

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:03.530
It's always a pleasure dealing with you.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:08.790
My congratulations on the 
founding of Hell's sales team.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:11.440
Haven't we heard this before?

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:17.190
For this occasion, I would like to present you 
with an animal that will be useful in...

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.690
Yay, what a success!

00:09:18.900 --> 00:09:20.090
Venus-san?

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:22.190
So then, that voice just now...

00:09:22.190 --> 00:09:26.970
A versatile animal that can be sent 
to both Earth and Hell would be swell.

00:09:26.970 --> 00:09:31.950
This birdie's trick. It's very 
good at imitating voices.

00:09:31.950 --> 00:09:34.710
Even Ueda-san was surprised.

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:37.580
Yes, I was really surprised.

00:09:37.950 --> 00:09:40.580
I honestly thought God was with us.

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:45.040
If you want to surprise people at an attraction,
you need sound effects, right?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.450
I made its throat muscles soft, so it 
can be super good at imitating voices.

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:53.050
Playing back message.

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.490
Wow, even the machine noises are perfect!

00:09:55.690 --> 00:09:58.560
But how did it learn God's voice?

00:09:58.560 --> 00:10:01.980
Remember when I took it out a bit in Hell?

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:04.780
It looks like it heard and 
memorized the voice then.

00:10:04.780 --> 00:10:06.750
I-I'm sorry! I was faking it!

00:10:07.510 --> 00:10:10.090
O-Oh, that was Neptune-san.

00:10:10.090 --> 00:10:12.120
That was not good for my heart...

00:10:12.330 --> 00:10:15.060
This baby can replay any sound!

00:10:15.060 --> 00:10:17.390
Since I took away the 
heavy teeth, it can fly,

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:21.390
so the "can go to both Earth and Hell"
 part is covered, too!

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.630
God has spoken!

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:29.880
Accepted!

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.650
<b>Accepted</b>

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:32.650
<b>Superb
 Lyrebird</b>

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.650
Yes!

00:10:32.650 --> 00:10:33.930
That's great!

00:10:33.930 --> 00:10:34.900
Well done!

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.270
I'm glad that's over.

00:10:36.270 --> 00:10:38.740
Now we can send it to Yokota-san, too.

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:42.400
Huh, that's an interesting bird.

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:44.080
The real one is here!

00:10:44.080 --> 00:10:47.410
Huh, that's an interesting bird.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.890
Who are you?

00:10:49.890 --> 00:10:51.030
Who am I?

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:52.600
I am you.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:57.290
Yay! Now I can play the "dark self 
that's buried deep within me" game!

00:10:57.300 --> 00:11:01.800
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:10:57.980 --> 00:11:01.010
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:16.320
<b>* There are various interpretations</b>

00:11:02.740 --> 00:11:05.230
Wow! So this is the undisputed 
champion of Earth!

00:11:05.230 --> 00:11:08.380
By the way, twelve meters seems quite large.

00:11:08.380 --> 00:11:11.420
I thought gravity made it impossible 
to stand if you're too big?

00:11:11.420 --> 00:11:16.310
That's true, but the tyrannosaurus 
is not as heavy as it looks.

00:11:16.310 --> 00:11:18.810
Oh, is it like a papier-mâché thing?

00:11:19.620 --> 00:11:21.070
Actually, quite close to that.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:24.430
Please consider the bird's 
respiratory organs.

00:11:21.070 --> 00:11:41.590
<b>Lung</b>

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.560
There are a lot of bags 
attached to that lung!

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:41.590
<b>Air Sacs</b>

00:11:26.560 --> 00:11:29.220
These are called air sacs, 
and are part of the

00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.940
respiratory system used for 
sending air into the lung.

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:35.490
This system is more efficient than 
just breathing with the lung.

00:11:35.490 --> 00:11:37.690
And something similar 
to the birds' air sacs—

00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:41.580
—was inside the tyrannosaurus, too?
 That's why it was light!

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:45.610
It would be inappropriate to compare 
life's wisdom to papier-mâché.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:51.240
How beautiful! A dragon of destruction 
that harbors the void in its body!

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.680
Suddenly, I have no idea 
what you're talking about.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:15.500
Hello, everyone—

00:12:16.710 --> 00:12:18.800
Oh, no, Shimoda-kun!

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:19.830
Are you all right?!

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:21.100
Ow...

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:23.330
Are you okay? Are you hurt?

00:12:23.330 --> 00:12:26.460
I'm okay. I just stepped on something...

00:12:26.460 --> 00:12:28.590
Oh, what's this?

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:33.990
I'm sorry. It's a mess because we're 
sorting through old designs right now.

00:12:36.380 --> 00:12:39.490
This creature must be a 
mascot for something!

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:41.880
What is this? It's so cute!

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:44.610
But I've never seen a creature like this before.

00:12:44.900 --> 00:12:46.360
What kind of animal is it?

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:47.680
Oh, that?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.820
It's a rejected rough 
draft from a while ago.

00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:52.280
That brings back memories.

00:12:52.280 --> 00:12:55.240
I remember now, that design 
used to look like this.

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.250
So this design was turned 
into something else?

00:13:00.950 --> 00:13:02.710
What could it be?

00:13:02.710 --> 00:13:04.010
Try guessing!

00:13:04.010 --> 00:13:06.000
Uh, can I have a hint?

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.620
Let's see... It's still cute now.

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:10.130
<i>Somewhat</i> cute.

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:12.010
Unfortunately, it can't be eaten.

00:13:12.010 --> 00:13:13.290
It's not a horse.

00:13:13.290 --> 00:13:14.510
Nor a snake.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.770
<i>Those were not hints.</i>

00:13:17.080 --> 00:13:19.460
I'm bad at quizzes.

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:22.350
Would it be possible to get 
some more helpful hints?

00:13:22.350 --> 00:13:23.980
Hm, let's see.

00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.780
Even though we have
 very different tastes,

00:13:25.780 --> 00:13:28.210
in this rare instance, we all like it.

00:13:28.210 --> 00:13:31.350
True, it might be a character 
we've all come to love.

00:13:31.350 --> 00:13:34.910
Then I wonder if it's a 
masterpiece that even I know about.

00:13:34.910 --> 00:13:37.460
If you didn't know about it,
it wouldn't be a quiz, right?

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.410
How big is it, roughly?

00:13:39.910 --> 00:13:42.170
About 170 centimeters?

00:13:42.170 --> 00:13:44.200
That's bigger than I expected!

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:47.910
Appearances often undergo 
changes from the rough draft...

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:51.170
Lovable, rather large... Like a lion?

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:52.780
Sorry.

00:13:52.780 --> 00:13:53.840
That's not it.

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:56.180
This is the original design for the lion.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:13:58.120
That's huge!

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.430
Wait, wheels?!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:03.110
The order was for a "male where 
only its appearance is impressive."

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:04.360
"Only"?

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:08.810
If the manliest male in the group gets 
all the females and gets to reproduce,

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:12.620
"Then why not just put all his skill points 
into looks and forget about the rest?"

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Kindness</b>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Looks</b>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Strength</b>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Intelligence</b>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:16.080
<b>Wealth</b>

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.190
the client said.

00:14:14.190 --> 00:14:16.070
The females can do the hunting.

00:14:16.070 --> 00:14:19.090
So while it was nice that we made him big,

00:14:19.090 --> 00:14:23.190
his movements got sluggish, so we 
turned his hind legs into wheels.

00:14:24.720 --> 00:14:27.960
<i>I guess he doesn't care about 
looks if it's not a horse.</i>

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.530
Are these wheels are functional 
and not just for decoration?

00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:33.600
Of course.

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:37.820
They were able to run across the savanna, 
up rocky hills, and over all sorts of terrain.

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.600
That sounds useful!

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:42.350
But there was an unexpected downside.

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:45.720
The wheels left tracks, and they were loud.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:49.500
They gave away the lion's position 
and made prey run away.

00:14:49.500 --> 00:14:50.830
I see.

00:14:50.830 --> 00:14:54.110
But that might be useful for driving 
prey where you want them to go.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:56.110
That's what we thought too, but...

00:14:56.350 --> 00:14:57.810
What are you talking about?

00:14:57.810 --> 00:15:00.210
The pitiable lion.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:04.300
Ah! You mean the one we set loose on Galapagos,

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:07.370
and was happily driving his prey around
 until he got stuck in a swamp.

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:11.440
He couldn't get out, and even 
though he was just a demo unit,

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:13.480
we still felt really bad for him.

00:15:13.480 --> 00:15:15.270
Is that when we scrapped the idea?

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:19.180
Now that I think about it, 
we might have acted a bit too hastily.

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:20.560
<i>A bit?</i>

00:15:20.560 --> 00:15:23.020
In the end, if appearance is all that matters,

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:26.050
we figured that his body doesn't 
have to be all that big.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.580
What do you mean?

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:30.280
We added a fluffy mane!

00:15:30.500 --> 00:15:32.930
Since it's <i>just</i> a fluffy mane,

00:15:32.930 --> 00:15:35.450
it's light, but still makes his 
body look cooler and bigger, right?

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:37.290
<b>Lion
Final Form</b>

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:40.330
We made it so that the more male 
hormone testosterone it has,

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:42.890
the more gorgeous the mane.

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:45.220
So that also works as the 
proof of an "impressive male."

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:47.680
On top of it, the mane also seemed 
to protect his neck.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:52.470
I see. So that's how you settled 
on the design for the lion.

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:53.680
Then that means this one...

00:15:53.950 --> 00:15:57.140
Since the antlers look similar,
 is it the deer?

00:15:57.420 --> 00:15:59.550
This is the original design for the deer.

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:02.740
It has a tree growing out of its head?!

00:16:02.740 --> 00:16:04.310
That's like something from a fairy tale!

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:08.680
We thought that giving it antlers that looked 
like a tree could be used for camouflage.

00:16:08.680 --> 00:16:10.880
That might have been a bit naïve.

00:16:10.880 --> 00:16:12.560
What was the problem?

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.490
When the antlers grew over 
the course of many years,

00:16:15.490 --> 00:16:17.540
they got unnecessarily big.

00:16:17.540 --> 00:16:19.070
That's so pretty!

00:16:19.780 --> 00:16:23.640
And then, when the female would pick 
a male with an impressive tree...

00:16:30.550 --> 00:16:34.160
A male whose antlers became thin 
was no longer desired at all.

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.760
Since the antlers were just as thin as 
real branches, they could break off easily.

00:16:37.760 --> 00:16:38.960
That poor guy!

00:16:38.960 --> 00:16:41.900
If the antlers take years to become impressive,

00:16:41.900 --> 00:16:44.120
it also takes years for them to grow back.

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:46.700
And during that entire time,
no female would want him.

00:16:46.700 --> 00:16:47.980
That poor guy!

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:51.710
That's why we made it so the 
antlers grow in new every year.

00:16:51.710 --> 00:16:54.950
This way he can re-enter the 
reproduction play-offs again!

00:16:54.950 --> 00:16:56.860
Reproduction play-offs?

00:16:56.860 --> 00:17:00.540
We went from branch-like 
antlers to simple, thick antlers!

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:03.220
Having them regrow every 
year sounds draining,

00:17:03.220 --> 00:17:05.220
but I guess there's an important reason for it.

00:17:05.220 --> 00:17:07.180
It's like a safety mechanism.

00:17:08.400 --> 00:17:12.490
Hm, so it's not the deer, either. 
Could I get another hint?

00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:14.270
It walks on two legs!

00:17:14.270 --> 00:17:16.750
Oh, that's a huge hint!

00:17:16.750 --> 00:17:20.620
Right, it's got wings! Could it be a bird?!

00:17:20.620 --> 00:17:25.200
Does that mean such a cute 
face is rat-a-tatting poop!?

00:17:25.200 --> 00:17:26.760
Cut that out!

00:17:26.760 --> 00:17:29.080
My birdies were like this 
from the beginning!

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:32.190
The fully-formed idea descended into me!

00:17:32.190 --> 00:17:33.760
I-I'm sorry.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:37.420
But I'm impressed you remembered 
pooping often to stay light.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:38.410
Well done.

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:41.020
It left an impression on me.

00:17:41.020 --> 00:17:45.460
To begin with, heavy antlers on 
a chubby body with tiny wings...

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:47.280
That's not going to fly.

00:17:47.550 --> 00:17:49.360
A bird's legs are light and thin.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:52.820
The arm muscle was moved down to 
the pectorals, to help move the wings!

00:17:52.820 --> 00:17:57.180
And so its arms were lost, 
but instead, it has a long neck.

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.180
It can move its head skillfully, right?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:02.560
Oh, so the long neck is 
like an arm replacement.

00:18:02.560 --> 00:18:03.880
Kind of like an elephant's trunk.

00:18:03.880 --> 00:18:05.820
And the real ones are tasty!

00:18:06.010 --> 00:18:10.710
But Jupiter-san, you said this 
animal doesn't get eaten, right?

00:18:10.710 --> 00:18:13.420
Does that mean it's not a herbivore?

00:18:13.420 --> 00:18:16.070
I heard carnivores taste bad...

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:17.700
Hm, not sure.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:19.770
I guess if you had to say, 
it <i>could</i> be a herbivore.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:21.950
I do vouch for its cuteness, though.

00:18:21.950 --> 00:18:25.670
Neptune-san says it's cute, 
so something fluffy?

00:18:25.670 --> 00:18:27.700
I can't say that it's fluffy.

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:31.030
But Shimoda-kun's really 
been doing his homework.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:32.180
Good job.

00:18:32.180 --> 00:18:34.460
You're actually listening to what we say.

00:18:34.460 --> 00:18:38.510
Well, it's always so interesting 
how you solve problems.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:42.850
But I still don't know what 
this rough draft was for.

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.910
It shoots beams from its eyes!

00:18:44.910 --> 00:18:46.880
Is there an animal like that?!

00:18:46.880 --> 00:18:48.860
Oh, is it the whale?!

00:18:49.370 --> 00:18:50.840
They do shoot beams.

00:18:51.130 --> 00:18:53.350
But sorry. Wrong.

00:18:53.350 --> 00:18:56.520
This pup uses the beams to scan designs.

00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:57.360
Scan?!

00:18:57.360 --> 00:18:59.880
And it prints out documents from its mouth!

00:18:59.880 --> 00:19:01.120
Prints out?!

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:03.360
And the antlers are a Wi-Fi antenna!

00:19:03.360 --> 00:19:05.110
That's a multi-function device, right?!

00:19:06.830 --> 00:19:09.460
Not quite, but it can do a lot of things.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:11.350
It's right there.

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:13.620
It's you.

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.170
Shimoda-kun, it's you.

00:19:19.510 --> 00:19:23.250
Wait, I was created here, 
by this design team?

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.590
Sorry.

00:19:25.590 --> 00:19:27.260
That's wrong!

00:19:28.550 --> 00:19:31.270
You're a regular creature, made by God.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:35.800
Before you came, we talked about 
making an assistant for Ueda-san.

00:19:35.800 --> 00:19:39.680
That's why we first came up with 
a helper mascot character.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:41.670
So that's why it looks like this.

00:19:41.670 --> 00:19:43.910
But it was big and got in the way.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:44.660
Eek!

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.080
Why did you make it so big?

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:50.420
Well, if it wasn't our size,
 it wasn't very practical.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:55.230
If it's too small, it can't even 
make copies or open doors.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:58.710
Well, it wasn't such a good design.

00:19:58.710 --> 00:20:00.970
The worst was its voice.

00:20:05.630 --> 00:20:07.560
How's your progress?

00:20:08.050 --> 00:20:09.670
How's your progress?

00:20:09.670 --> 00:20:12.050
If I could somehow get it by tomorrow...

00:20:12.280 --> 00:20:15.200
The client's been pressuring me, too.

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:20.320
<b>How's your progress?</b>

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.600
How's your progress?

00:20:16.600 --> 00:20:19.090
I really wonder who set it to that.

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:24.550
Anyway, in the end, you came to our company.

00:20:24.550 --> 00:20:28.070
You're the final version of 
that rough draft, Shimoda-kun.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.640
We all like you.

00:20:30.640 --> 00:20:33.330
Your handmade desserts are always tasty.

00:20:34.850 --> 00:20:40.490
I'm so happy that the design team 
I love so much was involved in my birth!

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:42.840
I will cherish this fact!

00:20:44.780 --> 00:20:48.690
When did he become so lovable, huh?

00:20:48.690 --> 00:20:49.710
Yeah, huh?

00:20:49.710 --> 00:20:52.020
I'd like to make merchandise of this guy!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:53.470
Do as you like.

00:20:54.790 --> 00:20:56.490
It was worth making that, huh?

00:20:56.490 --> 00:21:00.850
That enthusiasm and passion 
is what supports us.

00:21:02.650 --> 00:21:03.870
A new order!

00:21:04.940 --> 00:21:07.850
A bird that doesn't lay eggs!

00:21:07.850 --> 00:21:09.000
What?

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.120
Make it work, please.

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:16.780
Well, we're used to the client being 
unreasonable and making us do everything.

00:21:16.780 --> 00:21:18.370
I'm sorry about that.

00:21:18.720 --> 00:21:21.000
Birdies fall under your umbrella,
 right, Ven-chan?

00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.630
This is a hard one!

00:21:22.890 --> 00:21:24.810
I can help with its cuteness.

00:21:24.810 --> 00:21:26.630
I wonder what cute thing 
it should give birth to...

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:29.280
I hope it'll be something I can eat.

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:30.620
I'm excited!

00:21:30.620 --> 00:21:32.880
All right, I'm ready for anything!

00:21:32.880 --> 00:21:35.150
Then let's begin our meeting.

00:21:36.800 --> 00:21:39.900
I look forward to seeing what kind 
of animal this leads to!

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:05.670
Shimoda! Time to work!

00:22:05.670 --> 00:22:08.750
Y-Yes! Coming right away!
